[33m key       [0m: the string used to find the lookup value [0m
[33m sourceVar [0m: the variable containing the list of keys and values. IE: [0m
 [33mweekday.lookup[0m=[32m:mon:Monday:tue:Tuesday:wed:Wednesday:thu:Thursday:fri:Friday:sat:Saturday:sun:Sunday: [0m
[33m returnVar [0m: your custom return variable [0m
 Returns the first value following a matched key. [0m
 Default delimiter for [33mkey:value[0m pairs is the semicolon '[33m:[0m' [0m
   ! Key strings must be unique. The first match will always be treated as the Key [0m
     any subsequent matches will be disregarded - effectively treated as a value, not the key. [0m
     To prevent a value being indavertantly treated as the key if it is a match, it must [0m
     be positioned after the matching key. IE: [0m
